.IX Title "Encode::JISX0213 3"
.TH Encode::JISX0213 3 "2015-06-27" "perl v5.34.0" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
Encode::JISX0213 \- JIS X 0213 encodings
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 4
\&    use Encode::JISX0213;
\&    use Encode qw/encode decode/;
\&    $byte = encode("iso\-2022\-jp\-2004", $utf8);
\&    $utf8 = decode("iso\-2022\-jp\-2004", $byte);
.Ve
.SH "ABSTRACT"
.IX Header "ABSTRACT"
This module provides following encodings.
.PP
.Vb 5
\&  Canonical         Alias                         Description
\&  \-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-
\&  euc\-jis\-2004      qr/\ebeuc\-?(jis|jp)\-?2004$/i   8\-bit encoding
\&  iso\-2022\-jp\-2004  qr/\ebiso\-?2022\-?jp\-?2004$/i   7\-bit encoding
\&  \-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-
.Ve
.IP "\(bu" 4
About \*(L"shift encoding\*(R" see Encode::ShiftJIS2004.
.PP
Additionally, it provides encodings for older revision, \s-1JIS X 0213:2000:\s0
.PP
.Vb 8
\&  Canonical         Alias                         Description
\&  \-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-
\&  euc\-jisx0213      qr/\ebeucjisx0213$/i           8\-bit encoding
\&                    qr/\ebeuc.*jp[ \e\-]?(?:2000|2k)$/i
\&                    qr/\ebjp.*euc[ \e\-]?(2000|2k)$/i
\&                    qr/\ebujis[ \e\-]?(?:2000|2k)$/i
\&  iso\-2022\-jp\-3     qr/\ebiso\-?2022\-?jp\-?3$/i      7\-bit encoding
\&  \-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-
.Ve
.PP
and for transition from legacy standards:
.PP
.Vb 7
\&  Canonical         Alias                         Description
\&  \-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-
\&  x\-iso2022jp2004\-compatible                      See note.
\&                    qr/\ebiso\-?2022\-?jp\-?2004\-?compatible$/i
\&  x\-iso2022jp2004\-strict                          See note.
\&                    qr/\ebiso\-?2022\-?jp\-?2004\-?strict$/i
\&  \-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-
.Ve
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
To find out how to use this module in detail, see Encode.
.SS "Notes on Compatibility"
.IX Subsection "Notes on Compatibility"
To encode Unicode string to byte string,
\&\f(CW\*(C`x\-iso2022jp2004\-strict\*(C'\fR uses \s-1JIS X 0208\s0 as much as possible,
strictly conforming to \s-1JIS X 0213:2004\s0 Annex 2.
It is compatible to other encodings.
.PP
\&\f(CW\*(C`x\-iso2022jp2004\-compatible\*(C'\fR uses \s-1JIS X 0208\s0 for the bit combinations
co-existing on \s-1JIS X 0208\s0 and \s-1JIS X 0213\s0 plane 1.
It is \fInot\fR compatible to other encodings;
it had never been registered by any standards bodies.
.PP
However, to decode byte string to Unicode string,
encodings in the tables above
accept arbitrary sequences of both \s-1JIS X 0208\s0 and \s-1JIS X 0213.\s0
Exception is \f(CW\*(C`x\-iso2022jp2004\-strict\*(C'\fR:
It accepts only allowed \s-1JIS X 0208\s0 sequences.
.PP
\&\f(CW\*(C`euc\-jis\-2004\*(C'\fR and \f(CW\*(C`euc\-jisx0213\*(C'\fR contains \s-1JIS X 0213\s0 plane 2 along with
\&\s-1JIS X 0212\s0 in G3.
By this non-standard extension, they have forward compatibility with
EUC-JP (\s-1AJEC\s0) in case of decoding.
.SS "Comparison with Other Modules"
.IX Subsection "Comparison with Other Modules"
Encode::JIS2K provides \f(CW\*(C`euc\-jisx0213\*(C'\fR, \f(CW\*(C`iso\-2022\-jp\-3\*(C'\fR and
\&\f(CW\*(C`shift_jisx0213\*(C'\fR encodings.
\&\f(CW\*(C`euc\-jp\*(C'\fR in Encode::JP 1.64 or later can decode \f(CW\*(C`euc\-jisx0213\*(C'\fR
sequences.
They support earlier revision of standard, and lack function to encode
sequences with multiple Unicode characters such as
katakana with semi-voiced sound mark.
.PP
ShiftJIS::X0213::MapUTF provides \f(CW\*(C`shift_jisx0213\*(C'\fR and \f(CW\*(C`shift_jis\-2004\*(C'\fR.
It does not provide interface to contemporary Encode module.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\s-1JIS X 0213:2000\s0
\&\fI7ビット及び8ビットの2バイト情報交換用符号化拡張漢字集合\fR
(\fI7\-bit and 8\-bit double byte coded extended \s-1KANJI\s0 sets for information
interchange\fR),
and its amendment \s-1JIS X\s0 0213:2000/Amd.1:2004.
.PP
Encode, Encode::JP, Encode::ShiftJIS2004.
